'''Nevarro City'''<ref name="CE Expanded">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> was the [[capital]]<ref name="Chapter 21" /> city of the [[planet]]<ref name="Chapter 8" /> [[Nevarro]]. It contained a [[Nevarro bazaar|bazaar]], a [[cantina]], which was later converted to a [[Nevarro school|school]], an [[Imperial Remnant safe house|Imperial facility]],<ref name="Chapter 1" /> and the [[Twi'lek healing baths]].<ref name="Chapter 3" /> Underneath the city ran a [[Nevarro sewer|sewer]], where [[the Tribe]]'s [[Nevarro Mandalorian covert|covert]] was located.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> A [[Underground lava river|river]] of [[Magma|lava]] connected the city's sewers and the outside landscape.<ref name="Chapter 8" />

==History==
[[File:NevarroCity-TMCh12.png|thumb|left|200px|Carson Teva visits the city]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate}}</ref> a [[Clash on Nevarro|skirmish]] took place in the city between forces of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]'s [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] and a group of [[bounty hunter]]s led by [[Din Djarin]].<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> After they liberated Nevarro from the Imperial control Karga and Dune rebuilt the city, with him operating as a [[Magistrate]] and Dune as the local [[Marshal]]. Afterwards, the city became a respectable place for a variety of citizens. The city streets became teeming with vendors, gathering places, and potted plants, and a statue honoring [[IG-11]] was constructed.<ref name="Chapter 12" />

The city continued to thrive, and the planet became an independent trade anchor and Outer Rim [[Hyperspace route|Hyperlane]] port of the [[Hydian Way]]. A construction boom was going on in the city, and money was made from [[belters]] that mined the [[Nevarro system asteroid fields|asteroid fields]] at the edge of [[Nevarro system|Nevarro's system]]. [[Kowakian monkey-lizard]]s resided peacefully on trees instead of being roasted.<ref name="Chapter 17">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 17: The Apostate}}</ref>

Captain [[Gorian Shard]] and his [[pirate]] [[Gorian Shard's pirate crew|gang]] laid [[Pirate siege on Nevarro|siege]] to the city and briefly took control of it away from [[High Magistrate]] Karga. However, Shard and most of his gang were killed when Karga received aid from the [[Children of the Watch]] under [[Din Djarin]] and [[Lady]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]]. Together, they were able to take back control of the city. As a reward Karga ceded all land stretching from the western lava flats to [[Bulloch Canyon]] to the Mandalorians. While they didn't have a home planet, he told them that they now have a home on Nevarro, to which the townsfolk cheered and celebrate.<ref name="Chapter 21" />

